{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src -name '*.md'; cat ../agent-source/README.md; grep -n '\"'^func'\"\\\\|\"'^type'\"\\\\|\"'^const'\"' ../agent-source/epaxos/epaxos.go\"","aggregated_output":"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/SKILL.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/activity-classes.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/SKILL.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/guide.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/references/experiments.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/system.md\nSwiftPaxos: Fast Geo-Replicated State Machines\n==========\n<!-- [![Go Report Card](https://goreportcard.com/badge/github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos)](https://goreportcard.com/report/github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos) -->\n\nThis repository contains the prototype implementation of SwiftPaxos, a new state-machine replication protocol for geo-distributed systems.\nSwiftPaxos is a _faster Paxos without compromises_.\nIn the best case, it executes a state-machine command in two message delays (one round-trip), and three otherwise.\nSwiftPaxos was [presented](https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24/presentation/ryabinin) at the 21st USENIX Symposium on Networked Systems Design and Implementation ([NSDI '24](https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24)).\n\nInstallation\n------------\n\n    git clone https://github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos.git\n    cd swiftpaxos\n    go install github.com/imdea-software/swiftpaxos\n\nImplemented protocols\n---------------------\n\n|  Protocol               | Comments                                          |\n|-------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|\n| SwiftPaxos              | See our NSDI'24 [paper](https://www.usenix.org/conference/nsdi24/presentation/ryabinin) for the full details.|\n| Paxos                   | The classic Paxos protocol.                       |\n| N<sup>2</sup>Paxos      | All-to-all variant of Paxos.                      |\n| CURP                    | CURP implemented over N<sup>2</sup>Paxos.         |\n| Fast Paxos              | Fast Paxos with uncoordinated collision recovery. |\n| EPaxos                  | A [corrected][epaxos_correct] version of EPaxos.  |\n\nThis software is based on the [Egalitarian Paxos](https://github.com/otrack/epaxos) code base, as well as the corrections made [here](https://github.com/otrack/epaxos).\n\nUsage\n-----\n#### participants\nThere are three types of participants: *master*, *servers* and *clients*. \nThe servers and clients implement the protocol logic. \nThe master maintains the configuration of the system.\n\n#### deployment configuration\nTo setup a run, the participants read deployment configuration file. \nSee [aws.conf][config] for an example of configuration file for AWS EC2.\n\n#### launching a participant\n\nMaster:\n    \n    swiftpaxos -run master -config conf.conf\n\nServer:\n\n    swiftpaxos -run server -config conf.conf -alias server_name\n\nClient:\n\n    swiftpaxos -run client -config conf.conf -alias client_name\n\n#### command line options\n\n    -alias alias\n        An alias of this participant\n    -config file\n        Deployment config file (required)\n    -latency file\n        Latency config file\n    -log file\n        Path to the log file\n    -protocol protocol\n        Protocol to run. Overwrites protocol field of the config file\n    -quorum file\n        Quorum config file\n    -run participant\n        Run a participant\n\nSee [quorum.conf][quorum] and [latency.conf][latency] for an example of quorum and latency configuration files.\n\nFlint\n-----\n\nTo have an idea on how different replication protocols would compare, we wrote a tool named [Flint][flint]. \nFlint takes as input a set of AWS regions.\nIt computes the expected latencies and estimates how the protocols perform in such a deployment.\n\n[config]: aws.conf\n[epaxos_correct]: https://github.com/otrack/on-epaxos-correctness\n[quorum]: quorum.conf\n[latency]: latency.conf\n[flint]: https://github.com/vonaka/flint\n17:const MAX_INSTANCE = 10 * 1024 * 1024\n19:const MAX_DEPTH_DEP = 10\n20:const TRUE = uint8(1)\n21:const FALSE = uint8(0)\n22:const ADAPT_TIME_SEC = 10\n24:const COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD = 10 * 1e9 // 10 second(s)\n26:const BF_K = 4\n27:const BF_M_N = 32.0\n29:const HT_INIT_SIZE = 200000\n42:type Replica struct {\n88:type InstPair struct {\n93:type Instance struct {\n106:type instanceId struct {\n111:type LeaderBookkeeping struct {\n134:func New(alias string, id int, peerAddrList []string, exec, beacon, durable bool, batchWait int, transconf bool, failures int, conf *config.Config, logger *dlog.Logger) *Replica {\n199:func (r *Replica) recordInstanceMetadata(inst *Instance) {\n217:func (r *Replica) recordCommands(cmds []state.Command) {\n230:func (r *Replica) sync() {\n241:func (r *Replica) fastClock() {\n247:func (r *Replica) slowClock() {\n254:func (r *Replica) stopAdapting() {\n274:func (r *Replica) BatchingEnabled() bool {\n278:func (r *Replica) run() {\n385:func (r *Replica) executeCommands() {\n435:func isInitialBallot(ballot int32, replica int32, instance int32) bool {\n439:func (r *Replica) makeBallot(replica int32, instance int32) {\n453:func (r *Replica) replyPrepare(replicaId int32, reply *PrepareReply) {\n457:func (r *Replica) replyPreAccept(replicaId int32, reply *PreAcceptReply) {\n461:func (r *Replica) replyAccept(replicaId int32, reply *AcceptReply) {\n465:func (r *Replica) replyTryPreAccept(replicaId int32, reply *TryPreAcceptReply) {\n469:func (r *Replica) bcastPrepare(replica int32, instance int32) {\n494:func (r *Replica) bcastPreAccept(replica int32, instance int32) {\n528:func (r *Replica) bcastTryPreAccept(replica int32, instance int32) {\n555:func (r *Replica) bcastAccept(replica int32, instance int32) {\n589:func (r *Replica) bcastCommit(replica int32, instance int32) {\n613:func (r *Replica) clearHashtables() {\n619:func (r *Replica) updateCommitted(replica int32) {\n629:func (r *Replica) updateConflicts(cmds []state.Command, replica int32, instance int32, seq int32) {\n657:func (r *Replica) updateAttributes(cmds []state.Command, seq int32, deps []int32, replica int32, instance int32) (int32, []int32, bool) {\n693:func (r *Replica) mergeAttributes(seq1 int32, deps1 []int32, seq2 int32, deps2 []int32) (int32, []int32, bool) {\n715:func equal(deps1 []int32, deps2 []int32) bool {\n724:func (r *Replica) handlePropose(propose *defs.GPropose) {\n751:func (r *Replica) startPhase1(cmds []state.Command, replica int32, instance int32, ballot int32, proposals []*defs.GPropose) {\n781:func (r *Replica) handlePreAccept(preAccept *PreAccept) {\n847:func (r *Replica) handlePreAcceptReply(pareply *PreAcceptReply) {\n974:func (r *Replica) handleAccept(accept *Accept) {\n1008:func (r *Replica) handleAcceptReply(areply *AcceptReply) {\n1066:func (r *Replica) handleCommit(commit *Commit) {\n1121:func (r *Replica) BeTheLeader(args *defs.BeTheLeaderArgs, reply *defs.BeTheLeaderReply) error {\n1127:func (r *Replica) startRecoveryForInstance(replica int32, instance int32) {\n1171:func (r *Replica) handlePrepare(prepare *Prepare) {\n1204:func (r *Replica) handlePrepareReply(preply *PrepareReply) {\n1316:func (r *Replica) handleTryPreAccept(tpa *TryPreAccept) {\n1354:func (r *Replica) findPreAcceptConflicts(cmds []state.Command, replica int32, instance int32, seq int32, deps []int32) (bool, int32, int32) {\n1402:func (r *Replica) handleTryPreAcceptReply(tpar *TryPreAcceptReply) {\n1491:func updateDeferred(dr int32, di int32, r int32, i int32) {\n1497:func deferredByInstance(q int32, i int32) (bool, int32, int32) {\n1508:func (r *Replica) newInstanceDefault(replica int32, instance int32) *Instance {\n1512:func (r *Replica) newInstance(replica int32, instance int32, cmds []state.Command, cballot int32, lballot int32, status int8, seq int32, deps []int32) *Instance {\n1516:func (r *Replica) newLeaderBookkeepingDefault() *LeaderBookkeeping {\n1520:func (r *Replica) newLeaderBookkeeping(p []*defs.GPropose, originalDeps []int32, committedDeps []int32, deps []int32, lastTriedBallot int32, cmds []state.Command, status int8, seq int32) *LeaderBookkeeping {\n1524:func (r *Replica) newNilDeps() []int32 {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md; nl -ba ../agent-source/epaxos/epaxos.go | sed -n '29,240p;278,452p;724,1120p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/guide.md /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/references/behavior-facts.md; nl -ba ../agent-source/epaxos/epaxos.go | sed -n '29,240p;278,452p;724,1120p'\"","aggregated_output":"# Investigation and selection\n\nCandidate investigates a sourced question, including unknown requirements, protection premises or legal history. Obligation fixes an applicable responsibility without presuming violation; Check supplies inputs, history and observations. Missing authority calls for contract investigation, missing history for source work or conditional exploration. Neither gap bars a Candidate or licenses an invented obligation.\n\nFirst explain both core relationships from activity_roles and their connection in AuditSpec.core_overview. Follow representative work through owners, qualified support, aggregation, decision, propagation and consumption; explain acquisition, change and loss of context/authority and handling of old requests, replies, pending support and established decisions. Read the supporting membership, history, recovery and completion mechanisms needed for this backbone. Trace callers and callees, important rejection, retry and asynchronous paths; deeper variants may remain open.\n\nSave early discrepancies as sourced Surfaces or specific unknowns even when no obligation is ready. Distinguish open_details from core_gaps: unexplained formation, authority transition or old-work handling breaks readiness; a usable overview can retain local anomalies. Only a preconfigured directed_question permits a proportionate local boundary first; activity_focus does not. A usable map and first Candidate may share a product. Unmapped source work and exploration need no fabricated Fact.\n\nUse behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n\nUse question, counterevidence, unknowns, importance and trigger_rationale to identify what remains unexplained, what existing protection does establish, and what the next action will distinguish. A concise sourced difference suffices; no ranking, mandatory alternative list or confidence threshold. Compare contract reading, smaller exploration and another known relationship before committing to a costly test. “This input has not been run” alone is not a discriminator. An empty unknowns list does not disqualify a check whose earlier investigation established its value.\n\nWhen sourced mechanisms answer the specific suspicion, submit explained and reselect. An unconstructed single obligation may remain unexecuted; this is neither holds nor a budget refund. Fixed artifacts, directed execution tasks, changed premises and open disputes remain visible until explicitly handled. An explicit guard with unresolved ownership, timing, producer or context instead calls for investigation of that premise. A negative result should identify the plausible explanation it excluded and independent premises left open; distinguish it from execution corroborating an already-explained protection. Neither settles the entire Fact or becomes a reason to expand input variants indefinitely. Keep one requirement's independent scenarios together; a genuinely different responsibility gets its own question.\n\nConditional differences with unclear contracts remain exploration or local pause. Once responsibility is grounded, obligation and construction may be separate products. Reuse helpers and legal prefixes only after checking their entry, caller duties, completion order and fault assumptions for this question. A convenient driver must not exclude permitted overlap that supplied the discriminator, nor assume a looser ordering is legal because it produces a difference. Fixed checks must still exercise the investigated premise; a narrower child cannot settle its parent. Use existing F2/F3 when requirement or scope changes. Finish necessary technical repair and review of accepted work; switching questions preserves its debt.\n\nPrioritize consensus safety and explicitly scoped progress duties. Distinguish a sourced numeric/event deadline, implementation-owned automatic continuation without a numeric deadline, and later work explicitly owed by the caller. No numeric deadline does not preclude investigating lost continuation triggers; the word automatic alone supplies no obligation. A possible later event in a comment is not a guarantee that callers produce it. Independently grounded eligibility, accounting, wakeup or correlation duties can be resolved without a client endpoint or global consequence. Shared facts and helpers transfer understanding, not results.\n\nAt natural handoffs retain the answered proposition and remaining discriminator in feedback using tasks/audit.md references. In the next already-needed related map submission, replace the answered original unknown with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete progress reminders. Correct materially misleading higher-level summaries in that same product before reuse; harmless wording differences need no cleanup turn or whole-map sweep. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment, not an understanding label or reference alone. Use behavior-facts.md for primary ownership instead of copying one answer across layers. Source work and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning.\n\nOpen runs continue investigation until controller time/call or actual interruption boundaries. Empty pending_work or disposed registered questions does not exhaust the frontier: use the overview, other consumers/contexts, Surfaces and unread paths. Unit admission exhaustion still permits sourced Candidates, premise investigation and authorized exploration without immediate escalation. Follow each capacity separately; do not repeat handoffs, rerun explained guards, reuse an old Claim for a new proposition or refill budgets. Take a smaller informative step near expiry. Only a preconfigured finite directed task may complete early. Actual cancellation, safety refusal, permission loss and unrecoverable service/tool failure still stop.\n# Conditions, effects and semantic facts\n\nDescribe sourced owners, triggers, guards, state changes, effects and asynchronous boundaries. For a relevant relationship already read, identify who establishes the fact under which conditions and what its consumer actually requires. Include other read establishment, invalidation or reinterpretation paths; unread paths remain unknown or sourced Surfaces.\n\nShared updates do not imply shared follow-up effects. When one entry establishes a fact and schedules a consumer but another only establishes the fact, preserve that distinction in trigger, important_branches, writes, external_effects or async_boundaries. Do not union effects into an unconditional guarantee. Distinguish possible effects, conditional scheduling and guaranteed completion. A Behavior can cover multiple entries when conditions remain clear; split minimally when owners, completion boundaries or meanings cannot be expressed accurately together. Do not enumerate every branch or duplicate a shared Fact.\n\nFact states the assertion actually established for its identity and validity_context, not the strongest effect seen on any path. Reporting, internal accounting, notification and completed external work are distinct. Trace relevant guard inputs to their producer, update point, owner and completion duty instead of trusting a variable name. Conversely, a missing local field is not a missing guarantee when dispatch, admission, serialization or reset supplies it. Assess the composed producer/consumer protection, not each structure in isolation. Absent direct action is a question: inspect alternative consumers, delayed validation, shared scheduling and recovery for the same object and history before alleging a defect.\n\nUse produces_fact_ids/consumes_fact_ids for established relationships needed by later questions; reverse indexes are derived. No name-based edges, mandatory edges, branch fields or completeness scores. Reference validation proves structure, not equivalent path meaning. Guards and observed differences do not supply normative obligations without applicable sources and reasoning.\n\nUse existing map_changes at natural handoffs. Correcting an overstrong abstraction challenges the specific Candidate premise that depended on it; independent results retain their original basis. Use preserves only when requirements, dependencies and observation scope actually remain applicable. Meaning, identity, context and dependency changes cannot masquerade as clarification. No change means no version; keep history and counterevidence.\n\nKeep one primary home for each kind of knowledge: Behavior owns producer conditions, changes, synchronization, notification and exit mechanisms; Fact owns the assertion for its identity and validity_context; Candidate/feedback owns the question's answer, actual execution and remaining discriminator; Activity/core_overview owns the core connections, higher-level understanding and navigation; Surface owns unread entries and reasons; CheckRun/assessment/review owns experiment progress and judgments. Scope owns exclusions. Preserve substantive overviews without copying the same long answer and residuals through every layer. Mapped means association, not resolution. An explained Candidate needs no challenge merely to restate its protection; changed protection or Fact context does require attribution. Use the guide's natural handoff for answered unknowns and tasks/audit.md for Material and execution references.\n    29\tconst HT_INIT_SIZE = 200000\n    30\t\n    31\t// main differences with the original code base\n    32\t// - fix N=3 case\n    33\t// - add vbal variable (TLA spec. is wrong)\n    34\t// - remove checkpoints (need to fix them first)\n    35\t// - remove short commits (with N>7 propagating committed dependencies is necessary)\n    36\t// - must run with thriftiness on (recovery is incorrect otherwise)\n    37\t// - when conflicts are transitive skip waiting prior commuting commands\n    38\t\n    39\tvar cpMarker []state.Command\n    40\tvar cpcounter = 0\n    41\t\n    42\ttype Replica struct {\n    43\t\t*replica.Replica\n    44\t\tprepareChan           chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    45\t\tpreAcceptChan         chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    46\t\tacceptChan            chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    47\t\tcommitChan            chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    48\t\tprepareReplyChan      chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    49\t\tpreAcceptReplyChan    chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    50\t\tpreAcceptOKChan       chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    51\t\tacceptReplyChan       chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    52\t\ttryPreAcceptChan      chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    53\t\ttryPreAcceptReplyChan chan fastrpc.Serializable\n    54\t\tprepareRPC            uint8\n    55\t\tprepareReplyRPC       uint8\n    56\t\tpreAcceptRPC          uint8\n    57\t\tpreAcceptReplyRPC     uint8\n    58\t\tacceptRPC             uint8\n    59\t\tacceptReplyRPC        uint8\n    60\t\tcommitRPC             uint8\n    61\t\ttryPreAcceptRPC       uint8\n    62\t\ttryPreAcceptReplyRPC  uint8\n    63\t\t// the space of all instances (used and not yet used)\n    64\t\tInstanceSpace [][]*Instance\n    65\t\t// highest active instance numbers that this replica knows about\n    66\t\tcrtInstance []int32\n    67\t\t// highest committed instance per replica that this replica knows about\n    68\t\tCommittedUpTo []int32\n    69\t\t// instance up to which all commands have been executed (including iteslf)\n    70\t\tExecedUpTo       []int32\n    71\t\texec             *Exec\n    72\t\tconflicts        []map[state.Key]*InstPair\n    73\t\tmaxSeqPerKey     map[state.Key]int32\n    74\t\tmaxSeq           int32\n    75\t\tlatestCPReplica  int32\n    76\t\tlatestCPInstance int32\n    77\t\t// for synchronizing when sending replies to clients\n    78\t\t// from multiple go-routines\n    79\t\tclientMutex        *sync.Mutex\n    80\t\tinstancesToRecover chan *instanceId\n    81\t\t// does this replica think it is the leader\n    82\t\tIsLeader      bool\n    83\t\tmaxRecvBallot int32\n    84\t\tbatchWait     int\n    85\t\ttransconf     bool\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\ttype InstPair struct {\n    89\t\tlast      int32\n    90\t\tlastWrite int32\n    91\t}\n    92\t\n    93\ttype Instance struct {\n    94\t\tCmds           []state.Command\n    95\t\tbal, vbal      int32\n    96\t\tStatus         int8\n    97\t\tSeq            int32\n    98\t\tDeps           []int32\n    99\t\tlb             *LeaderBookkeeping\n   100\t\tIndex, Lowlink int\n   101\t\tbfilter        any\n   102\t\tproposeTime    int64\n   103\t\tid             *instanceId\n   104\t}\n   105\t\n   106\ttype instanceId struct {\n   107\t\treplica  int32\n   108\t\tinstance int32\n   109\t}\n   110\t\n   111\ttype LeaderBookkeeping struct {\n   112\t\tclientProposals   []*defs.GPropose\n   113\t\tballot            int32\n   114\t\tallEqual          bool\n   115\t\tpreAcceptOKs      int\n   116\t\tacceptOKs         int\n   117\t\tnacks             int\n   118\t\toriginalDeps      []int32\n   119\t\tcommittedDeps     []int32\n   120\t\tprepareReplies    []*PrepareReply\n   121\t\tpreparing         bool\n   122\t\ttryingToPreAccept bool\n   123\t\tpossibleQuorum    []bool\n   124\t\ttpaReps           int\n   125\t\ttpaAccepted       bool\n   126\t\tlastTriedBallot   int32\n   127\t\tcmds              []state.Command\n   128\t\tstatus            int8\n   129\t\tseq               int32\n   130\t\tdeps              []int32\n   131\t\tleaderResponded   bool\n   132\t}\n   133\t\n   134\tfunc New(alias string, id int, peerAddrList []string, exec, beacon, durable bool, batchWait int, transconf bool, failures int, conf *config.Config, logger *dlog.Logger) *Replica {\n   135\t\tr := &Replica{\n   136\t\t\treplica.New(alias, id, failures, peerAddrList, true, exec, false, conf, logger),\n   137\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   138\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   139\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   140\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   141\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   142\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE*3),\n   143\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE*3),\n   144\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE*2),\n   145\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   146\t\t\tmake(chan fastrpc.Serializable, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   147\t\t\t0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0,\n   148\t\t\tmake([][]*Instance, len(peerAddrList)),\n   149\t\t\tmake([]int32, len(peerAddrList)),\n   150\t\t\tmake([]int32, len(peerAddrList)),\n   151\t\t\tmake([]int32, len(peerAddrList)),\n   152\t\t\tnil,\n   153\t\t\tmake([]map[state.Key]*InstPair, len(peerAddrList)),\n   154\t\t\tmake(map[state.Key]int32),\n   155\t\t\t0,\n   156\t\t\t0,\n   157\t\t\t-1,\n   158\t\t\tnew(sync.Mutex),\n   159\t\t\tmake(chan *instanceId, defs.CHAN_BUFFER_SIZE),\n   160\t\t\tfalse,\n   161\t\t\t-1,\n   162\t\t\tbatchWait,\n   163\t\t\ttransconf,\n   164\t\t}\n   165\t\n   166\t\tr.Beacon = beacon\n   167\t\tr.Durable = durable\n   168\t\n   169\t\tfor i := 0; i < r.N; i++ {\n   170\t\t\tr.InstanceSpace[i] = make([]*Instance, MAX_INSTANCE) // FIXME\n   171\t\t\tr.crtInstance[i] = -1\n   172\t\t\tr.ExecedUpTo[i] = -1\n   173\t\t\tr.CommittedUpTo[i] = -1\n   174\t\t\tr.conflicts[i] = make(map[state.Key]*InstPair, HT_INIT_SIZE)\n   175\t\t}\n   176\t\n   177\t\tr.exec = &Exec{r}\n   178\t\n   179\t\tcpMarker = make([]state.Command, 0)\n   180\t\n   181\t\t//register RPCs\n   182\t\tr.prepareRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(Prepare), r.prepareChan)\n   183\t\tr.prepareReplyRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(PrepareReply), r.prepareReplyChan)\n   184\t\tr.preAcceptRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(PreAccept), r.preAcceptChan)\n   185\t\tr.preAcceptReplyRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(PreAcceptReply), r.preAcceptReplyChan)\n   186\t\tr.acceptRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(Accept), r.acceptChan)\n   187\t\tr.acceptReplyRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(AcceptReply), r.acceptReplyChan)\n   188\t\tr.commitRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(Commit), r.commitChan)\n   189\t\tr.tryPreAcceptRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(TryPreAccept), r.tryPreAcceptChan)\n   190\t\tr.tryPreAcceptReplyRPC = r.RPC.Register(new(TryPreAcceptReply), r.tryPreAcceptReplyChan)\n   191\t\n   192\t\tr.Stats.M[\"weird\"], r.Stats.M[\"conflicted\"], r.Stats.M[\"slow\"], r.Stats.M[\"fast\"], r.Stats.M[\"totalCommitTime\"], r.Stats.M[\"totalBatching\"], r.Stats.M[\"totalBatchingSize\"] = 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0\n   193\t\n   194\t\tgo r.run()\n   195\t\n   196\t\treturn r\n   197\t}\n   198\t\n   199\tfunc (r *Replica) recordInstanceMetadata(inst *Instance) {\n   200\t\tif !r.Durable {\n   201\t\t\treturn\n   202\t\t}\n   203\t\n   204\t\tb := make([]byte, 9+r.N*4)\n   205\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(b[0:4], uint32(inst.bal))\n   206\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(b[0:4], uint32(inst.vbal))\n   207\t\tb[4] = byte(inst.Status)\n   208\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(b[5:9], uint32(inst.Seq))\n   209\t\tl := 9\n   210\t\tfor _, dep := range inst.Deps {\n   211\t\t\tbinary.LittleEndian.PutUint32(b[l:l+4], uint32(dep))\n   212\t\t\tl += 4\n   213\t\t}\n   214\t\tr.StableStore.Write(b[:])\n   215\t}\n   216\t\n   217\tfunc (r *Replica) recordCommands(cmds []state.Command) {\n   218\t\tif !r.Durable {\n   219\t\t\treturn\n   220\t\t}\n   221\t\n   222\t\tif cmds == nil {\n   223\t\t\treturn\n   224\t\t}\n   225\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(cmds); i++ {\n   226\t\t\tcmds[i].Marshal(io.Writer(r.StableStore))\n   227\t\t}\n   228\t}\n   229\t\n   230\tfunc (r *Replica) sync() {\n   231\t\tif !r.Durable {\n   232\t\t\treturn\n   233\t\t}\n   234\t\n   235\t\tr.StableStore.Sync()\n   236\t}\n   237\t\n   238\tvar fastClockChan chan bool\n   239\tvar slowClockChan chan bool\n   240\t\n   278\tfunc (r *Replica) run() {\n   279\t\tr.ConnectToPeers()\n   280\t\n   281\t\tr.ComputeClosestPeers()\n   282\t\n   283\t\tif r.Exec {\n   284\t\t\tgo r.executeCommands()\n   285\t\t}\n   286\t\n   287\t\tslowClockChan = make(chan bool, 1)\n   288\t\tfastClockChan = make(chan bool, 1)\n   289\t\tgo r.slowClock()\n   290\t\n   291\t\tif r.BatchingEnabled() {\n   292\t\t\tgo r.fastClock()\n   293\t\t}\n   294\t\n   295\t\tif r.Beacon {\n   296\t\t\tgo r.stopAdapting()\n   297\t\t}\n   298\t\n   299\t\tonOffProposeChan := r.ProposeChan\n   300\t\n   301\t\tgo r.WaitForClientConnections()\n   302\t\n   303\t\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n   304\t\n   305\t\t\tselect {\n   306\t\n   307\t\t\tcase propose := <-onOffProposeChan:\n   308\t\t\t\tr.handlePropose(propose)\n   309\t\t\t\tif r.BatchingEnabled() {\n   310\t\t\t\t\tonOffProposeChan = nil\n   311\t\t\t\t}\n   312\t\t\t\tbreak\n   313\t\n   314\t\t\tcase <-fastClockChan:\n   315\t\t\t\tonOffProposeChan = r.ProposeChan\n   316\t\t\t\tbreak\n   317\t\n   318\t\t\tcase prepareS := <-r.prepareChan:\n   319\t\t\t\tprepare := prepareS.(*Prepare)\n   320\t\t\t\tr.handlePrepare(prepare)\n   321\t\t\t\tbreak\n   322\t\n   323\t\t\tcase preAcceptS := <-r.preAcceptChan:\n   324\t\t\t\tpreAccept := preAcceptS.(*PreAccept)\n   325\t\t\t\tr.handlePreAccept(preAccept)\n   326\t\t\t\tbreak\n   327\t\n   328\t\t\tcase acceptS := <-r.acceptChan:\n   329\t\t\t\taccept := acceptS.(*Accept)\n   330\t\t\t\tr.handleAccept(accept)\n   331\t\t\t\tbreak\n   332\t\n   333\t\t\tcase commitS := <-r.commitChan:\n   334\t\t\t\tcommit := commitS.(*Commit)\n   335\t\t\t\tr.handleCommit(commit)\n   336\t\t\t\tbreak\n   337\t\n   338\t\t\tcase prepareReplyS := <-r.prepareReplyChan:\n   339\t\t\t\tprepareReply := prepareReplyS.(*PrepareReply)\n   340\t\t\t\tr.handlePrepareReply(prepareReply)\n   341\t\t\t\tbreak\n   342\t\n   343\t\t\tcase preAcceptReplyS := <-r.preAcceptReplyChan:\n   344\t\t\t\tpreAcceptReply := preAcceptReplyS.(*PreAcceptReply)\n   345\t\t\t\tr.handlePreAcceptReply(preAcceptReply)\n   346\t\t\t\tbreak\n   347\t\n   348\t\t\tcase acceptReplyS := <-r.acceptReplyChan:\n   349\t\t\t\tacceptReply := acceptReplyS.(*AcceptReply)\n   350\t\t\t\tr.handleAcceptReply(acceptReply)\n   351\t\t\t\tbreak\n   352\t\n   353\t\t\tcase tryPreAcceptS := <-r.tryPreAcceptChan:\n   354\t\t\t\ttryPreAccept := tryPreAcceptS.(*TryPreAccept)\n   355\t\t\t\tr.handleTryPreAccept(tryPreAccept)\n   356\t\t\t\tbreak\n   357\t\n   358\t\t\tcase tryPreAcceptReplyS := <-r.tryPreAcceptReplyChan:\n   359\t\t\t\ttryPreAcceptReply := tryPreAcceptReplyS.(*TryPreAcceptReply)\n   360\t\t\t\tr.handleTryPreAcceptReply(tryPreAcceptReply)\n   361\t\t\t\tbreak\n   362\t\n   363\t\t\tcase beacon := <-r.BeaconChan:\n   364\t\t\t\tr.ReplyBeacon(beacon)\n   365\t\t\t\tbreak\n   366\t\n   367\t\t\tcase <-slowClockChan:\n   368\t\t\t\tif r.Beacon {\n   369\t\t\t\t\tr.Printf(\"weird %d; conflicted %d; slow %d; fast %d\\n\", r.Stats.M[\"weird\"], r.Stats.M[\"conflicted\"], r.Stats.M[\"slow\"], r.Stats.M[\"fast\"])\n   370\t\t\t\t\tfor q := int32(0); q < int32(r.N); q++ {\n   371\t\t\t\t\t\tif q == r.Id {\n   372\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   373\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   374\t\t\t\t\t\tr.SendBeacon(q)\n   375\t\t\t\t\t}\n   376\t\t\t\t}\n   377\t\t\t\tbreak\n   378\t\n   379\t\t\tcase iid := <-r.instancesToRecover:\n   380\t\t\t\tr.startRecoveryForInstance(iid.replica, iid.instance)\n   381\t\t\t}\n   382\t\t}\n   383\t}\n   384\t\n   385\tfunc (r *Replica) executeCommands() {\n   386\t\tconst SLEEP_TIME_NS = 1e6\n   387\t\tproblemInstance := make([]int32, r.N)\n   388\t\ttimeout := make([]uint64, r.N)\n   389\t\tfor q := 0; q < r.N; q++ {\n   390\t\t\tproblemInstance[q] = -1\n   391\t\t\ttimeout[q] = 0\n   392\t\t}\n   393\t\n   394\t\tfor !r.Shutdown {\n   395\t\t\texecuted := false\n   396\t\t\tfor q := int32(0); q < int32(r.N); q++ {\n   397\t\t\t\tfor inst := r.ExecedUpTo[q] + 1; inst <= r.crtInstance[q]; inst++ {\n   398\t\t\t\t\tif r.InstanceSpace[q][inst] != nil && r.InstanceSpace[q][inst].Status == EXECUTED {\n   399\t\t\t\t\t\tif inst == r.ExecedUpTo[q]+1 {\n   400\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.ExecedUpTo[q] = inst\n   401\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   402\t\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n   403\t\t\t\t\t}\n   404\t\t\t\t\tif r.InstanceSpace[q][inst] == nil || r.InstanceSpace[q][inst].Status < COMMITTED || r.InstanceSpace[q][inst].Cmds == nil {\n   405\t\t\t\t\t\tif inst == problemInstance[q] {\n   406\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttimeout[q] += SLEEP_TIME_NS\n   407\t\t\t\t\t\t\tif timeout[q] >= COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD {\n   408\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfor k := problemInstance[q]; k <= r.crtInstance[q]; k++ {\n   409\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.instancesToRecover <- &instanceId{q, k}\n   410\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   411\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttimeout[q] = 0\n   412\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   413\t\t\t\t\t\t} else {\n   414\t\t\t\t\t\t\tproblemInstance[q] = inst\n   415\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttimeout[q] = 0\n   416\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   417\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n   418\t\t\t\t\t}\n   419\t\t\t\t\tif ok := r.exec.executeCommand(int32(q), inst); ok {\n   420\t\t\t\t\t\texecuted = true\n   421\t\t\t\t\t\tif inst == r.ExecedUpTo[q]+1 {\n   422\t\t\t\t\t\t\tr.ExecedUpTo[q] = inst\n   423\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n   424\t\t\t\t\t}\n   425\t\t\t\t}\n   426\t\t\t}\n   427\t\t\tif !executed {\n   428\t\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n   429\t\t\t\tr.M.Unlock() // FIXME for cache coherence\n   430\t\t\t\ttime.Sleep(SLEEP_TIME_NS)\n   431\t\t\t}\n   432\t\t}\n   433\t}\n   434\t\n   435\tfunc isInitialBallot(ballot int32, replica int32, instance int32) bool {\n   436\t\treturn ballot == replica\n   437\t}\n   438\t\n   439\tfunc (r *Replica) makeBallot(replica int32, instance int32) {\n   440\t\tlb := r.InstanceSpace[replica][instance].lb\n   441\t\tn := r.Id\n   442\t\tif r.Id != replica {\n   443\t\t\tn += int32(r.N)\n   444\t\t}\n   445\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n   446\t\t\tfor n < r.maxRecvBallot {\n   447\t\t\t\tn += int32(r.N)\n   448\t\t\t}\n   449\t\t}\n   450\t\tlb.lastTriedBallot = n\n   451\t}\n   452\t\n   724\tfunc (r *Replica) handlePropose(propose *defs.GPropose) {\n   725\t\t//TODO!! Handle client retries\n   726\t\n   727\t\tbatchSize := len(r.ProposeChan) + 1\n   728\t\tr.M.Lock()\n   729\t\tr.Stats.M[\"totalBatching\"]++\n   730\t\tr.Stats.M[\"totalBatchingSize\"] += batchSize\n   731\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n   732\t\n   733\t\tr.crtInstance[r.Id]++\n   734\t\n   735\t\tcmds := make([]state.Command, batchSize)\n   736\t\tproposals := make([]*defs.GPropose, batchSize)\n   737\t\tcmds[0] = propose.Command\n   738\t\tproposals[0] = propose\n   739\t\tfor i := 1; i < batchSize; i++ {\n   740\t\t\tprop := <-r.ProposeChan\n   741\t\t\tcmds[i] = prop.Command\n   742\t\t\tproposals[i] = prop\n   743\t\t}\n   744\t\n   745\t\tr.startPhase1(cmds, r.Id, r.crtInstance[r.Id], r.Id, proposals)\n   746\t\n   747\t\tcpcounter += len(cmds)\n   748\t\n   749\t}\n   750\t\n   751\tfunc (r *Replica) startPhase1(cmds []state.Command, replica int32, instance int32, ballot int32, proposals []*defs.GPropose) {\n   752\t\t// init command attributes\n   753\t\tseq := int32(0)\n   754\t\tdeps := make([]int32, r.N)\n   755\t\tfor q := 0; q < r.N; q++ {\n   756\t\t\tdeps[q] = -1\n   757\t\t}\n   758\t\tseq, deps, _ = r.updateAttributes(cmds, seq, deps, replica, instance)\n   759\t\tcomDeps := make([]int32, r.N)\n   760\t\tfor i := 0; i < r.N; i++ {\n   761\t\t\tcomDeps[i] = -1\n   762\t\t}\n   763\t\n   764\t\tinst := r.newInstance(replica, instance, cmds, ballot, ballot, PREACCEPTED, seq, deps)\n   765\t\tinst.lb = r.newLeaderBookkeeping(proposals, deps, comDeps, deps, ballot, cmds, PREACCEPTED, -1)\n   766\t\tr.InstanceSpace[replica][instance] = inst\n   767\t\n   768\t\tr.updateConflicts(cmds, replica, instance, seq)\n   769\t\n   770\t\tif seq >= r.maxSeq {\n   771\t\t\tr.maxSeq = seq\n   772\t\t}\n   773\t\n   774\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.InstanceSpace[r.Id][instance])\n   775\t\tr.recordCommands(cmds)\n   776\t\tr.sync()\n   777\t\n   778\t\tr.bcastPreAccept(replica, instance)\n   779\t}\n   780\t\n   781\tfunc (r *Replica) handlePreAccept(preAccept *PreAccept) {\n   782\t\tinst := r.InstanceSpace[preAccept.Replica][preAccept.Instance]\n   783\t\n   784\t\tif preAccept.Seq >= r.maxSeq {\n   785\t\t\tr.maxSeq = preAccept.Seq + 1\n   786\t\t}\n   787\t\n   788\t\tif preAccept.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n   789\t\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = preAccept.Ballot\n   790\t\t}\n   791\t\n   792\t\tif preAccept.Instance > r.crtInstance[preAccept.Replica] {\n   793\t\t\tr.crtInstance[preAccept.Replica] = preAccept.Instance\n   794\t\t}\n   795\t\n   796\t\tif inst == nil {\n   797\t\t\tinst = r.newInstanceDefault(preAccept.Replica, preAccept.Instance)\n   798\t\t\tr.InstanceSpace[preAccept.Replica][preAccept.Instance] = inst\n   799\t\t}\n   800\t\n   801\t\tif inst != nil && preAccept.Ballot < inst.bal {\n   802\t\t\treturn\n   803\t\t}\n   804\t\n   805\t\tinst.bal = preAccept.Ballot\n   806\t\n   807\t\tif inst.Status >= ACCEPTED {\n   808\t\t\tif inst.Cmds == nil {\n   809\t\t\t\tr.InstanceSpace[preAccept.LeaderId][preAccept.Instance].Cmds = preAccept.Command\n   810\t\t\t\tr.updateConflicts(preAccept.Command, preAccept.Replica, preAccept.Instance, preAccept.Seq)\n   811\t\t\t\tr.recordCommands(preAccept.Command)\n   812\t\t\t\tr.sync()\n   813\t\t\t}\n   814\t\n   815\t\t} else {\n   816\t\t\tseq, deps, changed := r.updateAttributes(preAccept.Command, preAccept.Seq, preAccept.Deps, preAccept.Replica, preAccept.Instance)\n   817\t\t\tstatus := PREACCEPTED_EQ\n   818\t\t\tif changed {\n   819\t\t\t\tstatus = PREACCEPTED\n   820\t\t\t}\n   821\t\t\tinst.Cmds = preAccept.Command\n   822\t\t\tinst.Seq = seq\n   823\t\t\tinst.Deps = deps\n   824\t\t\tinst.bal = preAccept.Ballot\n   825\t\t\tinst.vbal = preAccept.Ballot\n   826\t\t\tinst.Status = status\n   827\t\n   828\t\t\tr.updateConflicts(preAccept.Command, preAccept.Replica, preAccept.Instance, preAccept.Seq)\n   829\t\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.InstanceSpace[preAccept.Replica][preAccept.Instance])\n   830\t\t\tr.recordCommands(preAccept.Command)\n   831\t\t\tr.sync()\n   832\t\n   833\t\t}\n   834\t\n   835\t\treply := &PreAcceptReply{\n   836\t\t\tpreAccept.Replica,\n   837\t\t\tpreAccept.Instance,\n   838\t\t\tinst.bal,\n   839\t\t\tinst.vbal,\n   840\t\t\tinst.Seq,\n   841\t\t\tinst.Deps,\n   842\t\t\tr.CommittedUpTo,\n   843\t\t\tinst.Status}\n   844\t\tr.replyPreAccept(preAccept.LeaderId, reply)\n   845\t}\n   846\t\n   847\tfunc (r *Replica) handlePreAcceptReply(pareply *PreAcceptReply) {\n   848\t\tinst := r.InstanceSpace[pareply.Replica][pareply.Instance]\n   849\t\tlb := inst.lb\n   850\t\n   851\t\tif pareply.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n   852\t\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = pareply.Ballot\n   853\t\t}\n   854\t\n   855\t\tif lb.lastTriedBallot > pareply.Ballot {\n   856\t\t\treturn\n   857\t\t}\n   858\t\n   859\t\tif lb.lastTriedBallot < pareply.Ballot {\n   860\t\t\tlb.nacks++\n   861\t\t\tif lb.nacks+1 > r.N>>1 {\n   862\t\t\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n   863\t\t\t\t\tr.makeBallot(pareply.Replica, pareply.Instance)\n   864\t\t\t\t\tr.bcastPrepare(pareply.Replica, pareply.Instance)\n   865\t\t\t\t}\n   866\t\t\t}\n   867\t\t\treturn\n   868\t\t}\n   869\t\n   870\t\tif lb.status != PREACCEPTED && lb.status != PREACCEPTED_EQ {\n   871\t\t\treturn\n   872\t\t}\n   873\t\n   874\t\tinst.lb.preAcceptOKs++\n   875\t\n   876\t\tif pareply.VBallot > lb.ballot {\n   877\t\t\tlb.ballot = pareply.VBallot\n   878\t\t\tlb.seq = pareply.Seq\n   879\t\t\tlb.deps = pareply.Deps\n   880\t\t\tlb.status = pareply.Status\n   881\t\t}\n   882\t\n   883\t\tisInitialBallot := isInitialBallot(lb.lastTriedBallot, pareply.Replica, pareply.Instance)\n   884\t\n   885\t\tseq, deps, allEqual := r.mergeAttributes(lb.seq, lb.deps, pareply.Seq, pareply.Deps)\n   886\t\tif r.N <= 3 && r.Thrifty {\n   887\t\t\t// no need to check for equality\n   888\t\t} else {\n   889\t\t\tinst.lb.allEqual = inst.lb.allEqual && allEqual\n   890\t\t\tif !allEqual {\n   891\t\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n   892\t\t\t\tr.Stats.M[\"conflicted\"]++\n   893\t\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n   894\t\t\t}\n   895\t\t}\n   896\t\n   897\t\tallCommitted := true\n   898\t\tif r.N > 7 {\n   899\t\t\tfor q := 0; q < r.N; q++ {\n   900\t\t\t\tif inst.lb.committedDeps[q] < pareply.CommittedDeps[q] {\n   901\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.committedDeps[q] = pareply.CommittedDeps[q]\n   902\t\t\t\t}\n   903\t\t\t\tif inst.lb.committedDeps[q] < r.CommittedUpTo[q] {\n   904\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.committedDeps[q] = r.CommittedUpTo[q]\n   905\t\t\t\t}\n   906\t\t\t\tif inst.lb.committedDeps[q] < inst.Deps[q] {\n   907\t\t\t\t\tallCommitted = false\n   908\t\t\t\t}\n   909\t\t\t}\n   910\t\t}\n   911\t\n   912\t\tif lb.status <= PREACCEPTED_EQ {\n   913\t\t\tlb.deps = deps\n   914\t\t\tlb.seq = seq\n   915\t\t}\n   916\t\n   917\t\tprecondition := inst.lb.allEqual && allCommitted && isInitialBallot\n   918\t\n   919\t\tif inst.lb.preAcceptOKs >= (r.Replica.FastQuorumSize()-1) && precondition {\n   920\t\t\tlb.status = COMMITTED\n   921\t\n   922\t\t\tinst.Status = lb.status\n   923\t\t\tinst.bal = lb.ballot\n   924\t\t\tinst.Cmds = lb.cmds\n   925\t\t\tinst.Deps = lb.deps\n   926\t\t\tinst.Seq = lb.seq\n   927\t\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(inst)\n   928\t\t\tr.sync()\n   929\t\n   930\t\t\tr.updateCommitted(pareply.Replica)\n   931\t\t\tif inst.lb.clientProposals != nil && !r.Dreply {\n   932\t\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(inst.lb.clientProposals); i++ {\n   933\t\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(\n   934\t\t\t\t\t\t&defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n   935\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTRUE,\n   936\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].CommandId,\n   937\t\t\t\t\t\t\tstate.NIL(),\n   938\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].Timestamp},\n   939\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].Reply,\n   940\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].Mutex)\n   941\t\t\t\t}\n   942\t\t\t}\n   943\t\n   944\t\t\tr.bcastCommit(pareply.Replica, pareply.Instance)\n   945\t\n   946\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n   947\t\t\tr.Stats.M[\"fast\"]++\n   948\t\t\tif inst.proposeTime != 0 {\n   949\t\t\t\tr.Stats.M[\"totalCommitTime\"] += int(time.Now().UnixNano() - inst.proposeTime)\n   950\t\t\t}\n   951\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n   952\t\t} else if inst.lb.preAcceptOKs >= r.Replica.FastQuorumSize()-1 {\n   953\t\t\tlb.status = ACCEPTED\n   954\t\n   955\t\t\tinst.Status = lb.status\n   956\t\t\tinst.bal = lb.ballot\n   957\t\t\tinst.Cmds = lb.cmds\n   958\t\t\tinst.Deps = lb.deps\n   959\t\t\tinst.Seq = lb.seq\n   960\t\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(inst)\n   961\t\t\tr.sync()\n   962\t\n   963\t\t\tr.bcastAccept(pareply.Replica, pareply.Instance)\n   964\t\n   965\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n   966\t\t\tr.Stats.M[\"slow\"]++\n   967\t\t\tif !allCommitted {\n   968\t\t\t\tr.Stats.M[\"weird\"]++\n   969\t\t\t}\n   970\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n   971\t\t}\n   972\t}\n   973\t\n   974\tfunc (r *Replica) handleAccept(accept *Accept) {\n   975\t\tinst := r.InstanceSpace[accept.Replica][accept.Instance]\n   976\t\n   977\t\tif accept.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n   978\t\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = accept.Ballot\n   979\t\t}\n   980\t\n   981\t\tif accept.Instance > r.crtInstance[accept.Replica] {\n   982\t\t\tr.crtInstance[accept.Replica] = accept.Instance\n   983\t\t}\n   984\t\n   985\t\tif inst == nil {\n   986\t\t\tinst = r.newInstanceDefault(accept.Replica, accept.Instance)\n   987\t\t\tr.InstanceSpace[accept.Replica][accept.Instance] = inst\n   988\t\t}\n   989\t\n   990\t\tif accept.Ballot < inst.bal {\n   991\t\t\tr.Printf(\"Smaller ballot %d < %d\\n\", accept.Ballot, inst.bal)\n   992\t\t} else if inst.Status >= COMMITTED {\n   993\t\t\tr.Printf(\"Already committed / executed \\n\")\n   994\t\t} else {\n   995\t\t\tinst.Deps = accept.Deps\n   996\t\t\tinst.Seq = accept.Seq\n   997\t\t\tinst.bal = accept.Ballot\n   998\t\t\tinst.vbal = accept.Ballot\n   999\t\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.InstanceSpace[accept.Replica][accept.Instance])\n  1000\t\t\tr.sync()\n  1001\t\t}\n  1002\t\n  1003\t\treply := &AcceptReply{accept.Replica, accept.Instance, inst.bal}\n  1004\t\tr.replyAccept(accept.LeaderId, reply)\n  1005\t\n  1006\t}\n  1007\t\n  1008\tfunc (r *Replica) handleAcceptReply(areply *AcceptReply) {\n  1009\t\tinst := r.InstanceSpace[areply.Replica][areply.Instance]\n  1010\t\tlb := inst.lb\n  1011\t\n  1012\t\tif areply.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n  1013\t\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = areply.Ballot\n  1014\t\t}\n  1015\t\n  1016\t\tif lb.status != ACCEPTED {\n  1017\t\t\treturn\n  1018\t\t}\n  1019\t\n  1020\t\tif lb.lastTriedBallot != areply.Ballot {\n  1021\t\t\treturn\n  1022\t\t}\n  1023\t\n  1024\t\tif areply.Ballot > lb.lastTriedBallot {\n  1025\t\t\tlb.nacks++\n  1026\t\t\tif lb.nacks+1 > r.N>>1 {\n  1027\t\t\t\tif r.IsLeader {\n  1028\t\t\t\t\tr.makeBallot(areply.Replica, areply.Instance)\n  1029\t\t\t\t\tr.bcastPrepare(areply.Replica, areply.Instance)\n  1030\t\t\t\t}\n  1031\t\t\t}\n  1032\t\t\treturn\n  1033\t\t}\n  1034\t\n  1035\t\tinst.lb.acceptOKs++\n  1036\t\n  1037\t\tif inst.lb.acceptOKs+1 > r.N/2 {\n  1038\t\t\tlb.status = COMMITTED\n  1039\t\t\tinst.Status = COMMITTED\n  1040\t\t\tr.updateCommitted(areply.Replica)\n  1041\t\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(inst)\n  1042\t\t\tr.sync()\n  1043\t\n  1044\t\t\tif inst.lb.clientProposals != nil && !r.Dreply {\n  1045\t\t\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(inst.lb.clientProposals); i++ {\n  1046\t\t\t\t\tr.ReplyProposeTS(\n  1047\t\t\t\t\t\t&defs.ProposeReplyTS{\n  1048\t\t\t\t\t\t\tTRUE,\n  1049\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].CommandId,\n  1050\t\t\t\t\t\t\tstate.NIL(),\n  1051\t\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].Timestamp},\n  1052\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].Reply,\n  1053\t\t\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals[i].Mutex)\n  1054\t\t\t\t}\n  1055\t\t\t}\n  1056\t\n  1057\t\t\tr.bcastCommit(areply.Replica, areply.Instance)\n  1058\t\t\tr.M.Lock()\n  1059\t\t\tif inst.proposeTime != 0 {\n  1060\t\t\t\tr.Stats.M[\"totalCommitTime\"] += int(time.Now().UnixNano() - inst.proposeTime)\n  1061\t\t\t}\n  1062\t\t\tr.M.Unlock()\n  1063\t\t}\n  1064\t}\n  1065\t\n  1066\tfunc (r *Replica) handleCommit(commit *Commit) {\n  1067\t\tinst := r.InstanceSpace[commit.Replica][commit.Instance]\n  1068\t\n  1069\t\tif commit.Instance > r.crtInstance[commit.Replica] {\n  1070\t\t\tr.crtInstance[commit.Replica] = commit.Instance\n  1071\t\t}\n  1072\t\n  1073\t\tif commit.Ballot > r.maxRecvBallot {\n  1074\t\t\tr.maxRecvBallot = commit.Ballot\n  1075\t\t}\n  1076\t\n  1077\t\tif inst == nil {\n  1078\t\t\tr.InstanceSpace[commit.Replica][commit.Instance] = r.newInstanceDefault(commit.Replica, commit.Instance)\n  1079\t\t\tinst = r.InstanceSpace[commit.Replica][commit.Instance]\n  1080\t\t}\n  1081\t\n  1082\t\tif inst.Status >= COMMITTED {\n  1083\t\t\treturn\n  1084\t\t}\n  1085\t\n  1086\t\tif commit.Ballot < inst.bal {\n  1087\t\t\treturn\n  1088\t\t}\n  1089\t\n  1090\t\t// FIXME timeout on client side?\n  1091\t\tif commit.Replica == r.Id {\n  1092\t\t\tif len(commit.Command) == 1 && commit.Command[0].Op == state.NONE && inst.lb.clientProposals != nil {\n  1093\t\t\t\tfor _, p := range inst.lb.clientProposals {\n  1094\t\t\t\t\tr.Printf(\"In %d.%d, re-proposing %s \\n\", commit.Replica, commit.Instance, p.Command.String())\n  1095\t\t\t\t\tr.ProposeChan <- p\n  1096\t\t\t\t}\n  1097\t\t\t\tinst.lb.clientProposals = nil\n  1098\t\t\t}\n  1099\t\t}\n  1100\t\n  1101\t\tinst.bal = commit.Ballot\n  1102\t\tinst.vbal = commit.Ballot\n  1103\t\tinst.Cmds = commit.Command\n  1104\t\tinst.Seq = commit.Seq\n  1105\t\tinst.Deps = commit.Deps\n  1106\t\tinst.Status = COMMITTED\n  1107\t\n  1108\t\tr.updateConflicts(commit.Command, commit.Replica, commit.Instance, commit.Seq)\n  1109\t\tr.updateCommitted(commit.Replica)\n  1110\t\tr.recordInstanceMetadata(r.InstanceSpace[commit.Replica][commit.Instance])\n  1111\t\tr.recordCommands(commit.Command)\n  1112\t\n  1113\t}\n  1114\t\n  1115\t/**********************************************************************\n  1116\t\n  1117\t                     RECOVERY ACTIONS\n  1118\t\n  1119\t***********************************************************************/\n  1120\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The ordinary path uses per-instance ballots and dependency attributes to form decisions. I also found three discrepancies to retain: Accept updates attributes without assigning ACCEPTED status, persistence writes both ballots to the same byte range, and the higher-ballot AcceptReply retry branch follows a guard that rejects it. I’ll trace recovery and the callers before judging their consequences.\n"}}
